<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30039" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŭrĭa</span></b> , ae
		(collat. form <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mŭrĭes</span></b> , ēi. v infra), f.
		
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁλμυοίς</span>
		, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>salt
				liquor, brine</i>, 
			
			<i>pickle</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleae conduntur vel virides in muriā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R. 7</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oleae ex muriā durā,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels. 4,
					9</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dura,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 4,
					15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ut melius muriā, quam testa marina
					remittat,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 2, 8, 53</span></i>
			.—Form muries, <i><span class="en">Cato, R. R.
				88, 2</span></i>; Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest.
				p. 158 sq.</span></i> Müll.; Fab. Pict. ap.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 223, 17</span></i>.</div>
